# Clauses no run states

clause Input and output contract: unfixturable, the heading opens straight onto the rules beneath it
    each rule beneath it states its own outcome and carries its own clause
clause Resolution sequence: unfixturable, the heading opens straight onto the numbered steps beneath it
    each step beneath it states its own outcome and carries its own clause
clause Parser and source-preserving edits: unfixturable, its prose binds how a build identifies and edits the spans of a source rather than what a run emits
    the invariants state what those means must produce, each carrying its own clause
clause Parser and source-preserving edits — Parsing authority: unfixturable, it binds what the reading of a source is let identify
    the rules governing what a bundle carries state the outcome, each carrying its own clause
clause Parser and source-preserving edits — Source positions: unfixturable, it binds how the spans of a source are built and retained
    the invariants a candidate is held to state what those spans must produce, each carrying its own clause
clause Parser and source-preserving edits — Source model: unfixturable, it binds what a build derives from the stream it reads
    the selection, boundary and destination rules state the outcome that derivation reaches, each carrying its own clause
clause Parser and source-preserving edits — Edits: unfixturable, it binds how edits are applied and how overlapping ones are resolved
    the bytes a bundle carries state the outcome, under the rules governing that content
clause Parser and source-preserving edits — Validation: unfixturable, it requires the candidate be read again and the declared invariants checked
    each invariant states its own outcome and carries its own clause
clause Mandatory parser viability gates: unfixturable, it states when its gates apply, before a production reading of sources is selected or any bundle is published
    the gates are met in choosing that reading rather than by any run over a source tree
clause Explicitly linked source structure: unfixturable, it states how sources are to be authored
    the rules beneath it state what a run does with sources so authored, each carrying its own clause
clause Explicitly linked source structure — Reading versus execution: unfixturable, it holds that inclusion makes material available without authorizing its execution, which no bundle's bytes show
    the authored instructions carry the execution verbs and the call boundaries that state it
clause Heading-only structural ancestors — Provenance: unfixturable, it requires ancestry be recorded apart from selected content, which a bundle states nothing of on its own
    the depth and deduplication rules state its effects, each carrying its own clause
clause Agent delivery contract: unfixturable, it states what a successful compilation does and does not establish about a transport
    a run produces a bundle and an exit status, and neither states what a transport delivered
clause Agent delivery contract — Response limit: unfixturable, it binds the calling wrapper's buffering and the response size it enforces
    observable once a consumer of the run's output is declared beside the source tree
clause Agent delivery contract — Broken pipes: unfixturable, it binds the wrapper's reporting of a transport failure
    a fixture declares a source tree and an invocation, and reaches no consumer of the run's output
clause Adversarial acceptance fixtures: unfixturable, it instructs that a corpus be written before broad implementation
    the corpus this report reads is what states it

